:name: head_unit
:description: head_unit (STM32H747I-DISCO + 800x480 panel) running our firmware, with the UI assets on an emulated SD card and its BLE radio: an nRF52840 running Zephyr's hci_uart, over HCI-UART.
:
:Build first and set $bin, $sdcard (head_unit's zephyr.elf and
:zephyr.sdcard.img) and $hci_bin (build/hci_uart/zephyr/zephyr.elf) -- see
:README.md for the full commands. (No defaults: Renode does not expand
:$ORIGIN in the SD card path.)
:
:head_unit's CPU is held until the controller has had 1 s to set up its
:UART, as in Renode's own HCI-UART demo; `runMacro $power_on_head_unit`
:releases it. No sensor here -- live_wind.resc adds one.

emulation CreateUARTHub "hci"
emulation CreateBLEMedium "wireless"

# BLE needs frequent synchronisation between machines.
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.00001"

using sysbus

mach create "controller"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nrf52840dk_nrf52840.repl
connector Connect sysbus.radio wireless
connector Connect sysbus.uart1 hci
sysbus LoadELF $hci_bin

mach create "head_unit"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32h747-disco.repl
machine SdCardFromFile $sdcard sysbus.sdmmc 0x800000 false
connector Connect sysbus.uart8 hci

# Match the real board's timing (Renode model gaps):
# - Renode's RCC model leaves SysTick at 128 MHz although Zephyr runs the
#   core at 400 MHz from the PLL, so uptime, timers and timeouts ran
#   3.125x slow. Set 400 MHz once the SysTick driver starts, after the
#   clocks are configured.
# - The CPU model defaults to 100 MIPS; the 400 MHz Cortex-M7 does about
#   400, which sets how long grvl's software rendering takes.
cpu PerformanceInMips 400

set systick_at_400mhz
"""
machine["sysbus.nvic"].Frequency = 400000000
"""

sysbus LoadELF $bin
cpu AddHook `sysbus GetSymbolAddress "sys_clock_driver_init"` $systick_at_400mhz
cpu IsHalted true

macro power_on_head_unit
"""
    mach set "head_unit"
    cpu IsHalted false
"""
